  "title": "Unified title",
  "summary": "This report presents a comprehensive review of threats targeting Voice Authentication Systems (VAS) and Anti-Spoofing Countermeasures (CMs), including data poisoning, adversarial attacks, deepfake, and adversarial spoofing. It highlights the evolution of these threats and the need for improved security postures.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "The GAHR framework combines generativity with veracity reasoning to improve detection accuracy, while the ELERF and RAEGNet models address limitations in existing detection methods.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "ClusterVAD, an unsupervised VAD built on frozen speech foundation model representations, clusters speech and non-speech with sonority and achieves threshold-free detection across various speech conditions.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The E5-large LLM performs best on both context-enriched and non-context-enriched classification tasks, demonstrating the potential of multilingual LLMs for scalable detection of hateful and constructive speech across languages.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
